WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.251
Canada's prime minister, just

00:00:01.251 --> 00:00:02.085
accused India

00:00:02.085 --> 00:00:03.753
of assassinating somebody

00:00:03.753 --> 00:00:05.255
on Canadian soil.

00:00:05.255 --> 00:00:06.256
[TRUDEAU] potential link

00:00:06.256 --> 00:00:08.717
between agents of the government of India

00:00:08.717 --> 00:00:10.927
and the killing of a Canadian citizen.

00:00:10.927 --> 00:00:12.512
Let me explain why this is a big deal.

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:13.221
Hardeep Singh

00:00:13.221 --> 00:00:15.682
Nijjar moved to Canada from India

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:16.349
and was a leader

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.976
of the Khalistan movement,

00:00:17.976 --> 00:00:18.435
an effort

00:00:18.435 --> 00:00:19.936
to create an independent state

00:00:19.936 --> 00:00:20.895
for Sikhs,

00:00:20.895 --> 00:00:23.023
a religious minority in northern India.

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:24.315
The Indian government called this guy

00:00:24.315 --> 00:00:25.191
a terrorist

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.317
and has been trying to arrest him

00:00:26.317 --> 00:00:27.110
for years.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:29.112
Nijjar found refuge in Canada,

00:00:29.112 --> 00:00:31.072
where nearly a million Sikhs live.

00:00:31.072 --> 00:00:31.364
That is,

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:32.282
until recently,

00:00:32.282 --> 00:00:34.034
when he was gunned down by two men

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:35.785
outside of a temple in Vancouver.

00:00:35.785 --> 00:00:37.537
India denied any involvement in this,

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:38.955
but Justin Trudeau's accusation

00:00:38.955 --> 00:00:40.206
that India was involved

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.249
means that there's at least

00:00:41.249 --> 00:00:42.625
some credible evidence here.

00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:44.002
But we just don't know yet.

00:00:44.002 --> 00:00:44.878
The whole thing is causing

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:45.628
some real tension

00:00:45.628 --> 00:00:46.713
between the two countries.

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.173
And it's right at a time

00:00:48.173 --> 00:00:49.466
when the West is trying

00:00:49.466 --> 00:00:50.133
to strengthen

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:51.342
its relationship with India

00:00:51.342 --> 00:00:52.302
as part of its efforts

00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:53.762
to counterbalance China.

00:00:53.762 --> 00:00:55.180
So I guess now we just wait

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:56.848
and see what evidence comes out.

00:00:56.848 --> 00:00:57.807
If you want to better understand

00:00:57.807 --> 00:00:59.601
global politics, follow for more.

